From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: share the H713 polyphase scaler between H.264 and HEVC

H264ConfigNewScaler in H713's vendor decoder routes H.264 through the same
VE+0xf00 4-tap/32-phase filter as HEVC. It needs H264_CTRL bit 11 and
VE_CHROMA_BUF_LEN bit 29, not the SDROT enable bit. Preserve full-size
reconstruction and replace the H.264 shifter with this path.

Allocate the scaler line buffer per decoder context, program geometry and
both coefficient banks per picture, and gate the new datapath to H713.
Remove the rotate control; no rotation is exposed for either codec.

Let NV12 CAPTURE S_FMT choose even output dimensions between 1x and 4x
per axis. Keep COMPOSE as an active rectangle in the negotiated canvas,
honour LE/GE constraints, and leave TRY_FMT free of side effects. Scaled
heights need only be even. A 32-byte secondary pitch keeps HEVC chroma
64-byte aligned; Main10 rounds packed 2-bit widths up before alignment.
Refresh reconstruction side-plane sizing when an early SPS declares Main10.

Coefficient generation is unchanged. Hardware validation and reproduction
commands are documented in docs/handoff-2026-09-17-shared-scaler.md.

Origin: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/blob/43b2cdd4aa1b161a281db8b10f02ce70085e2d42/patches/kernel/0120-media-cedrus-share-the-polyphase-scaler-with-h264.patch (0120-media-cedrus-share-the-polyphase-scaler-with-h264.patch, commit a861df2)
