-/*
- * The rotator lives in the H.264 engine, so a rotation requested while another
- * codec is selected is remembered but inert. Everything that ACTS on rotation
- * reads it through here rather than touching ctx->rotation directly, so a
- * stale request can never arm the H.264 transform path under MPEG-2, HEVC or
- * VP8. Storing it unconditionally is deliberate: rejecting the value in
- * s_ctrl instead broke the control framework's own range probing.
